# netsurf: element.style grid setters on the shared prototype -- fixes a 348 regression (patch 350)
# Generated 2026-10-30
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 349)
#
# 348 added 18 grid-related camelCase names to the element style object's
# per-instance setter list. Each style object then built ~36 more getter
# and setter closures. theguardian.com touches .style on enough elements
# to run the JS heap out: innerText threw "InternalError: out of memory",
# the textContent fallback failed with it, and the scorecard read the page
# as empty (guardian 81.7 -> 36.1). The gate has no page that big. A
# fresh scorecard caught it, and a bisect of 348's two halves pinned it to
# this file.
#
#  - macsurf_qjs.c: the 348 names come off the per-instance PS list. They
#    are defined once, on CSSStyleDeclaration.prototype (which every style
#    object gets, patch 280), and go through the instance's own
#    setProperty/getPropertyValue.
#
# Gate: CSS-grid-inline-placement still GRIDINL348 8/8. Scorecard:
# guardian back to 80.9 (text 0.995), twice.
--- a/content/handlers/javascript/quickjs/macsurf_qjs.c
+++ b/content/handlers/javascript/quickjs/macsurf_qjs.c
@@ -8770,6 +8770,26 @@
